    "rationale": "A reports no significant relationship between daily metformin dose and vitamin-B12 deficiency. B's extracted finding is about duration of metformin use (OR 1.01, 95% CI 1.00-1.02), which is a different exposure from dose, so the two findings answer different questions. B's abstract also reports a metformin dose association (OR 1.002; adjusted OR 4.10 for dose above the median), which would have been the matching finding. After adjustment, only dose above the median remained associated in B; the extracted duration finding is correctly labelled unadjusted. B's extraction omits the OR point estimate (1.01) and the authors' significance statement (\"statistically associated\"). It also omits the location (Vinmec Central Park Hospital, Vietnam) and the dose and duration thresholds (1000 mg/day or more, 48 months or more). These omissions do not change the finding."
